<title>USA: Swiss Army Brands Inc Q4 loss from charge.</title>
<headline>Swiss Army Brands Inc Q4 loss from charge.</headline>
<dateline>SHELTON, Conn. 1997-02-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>(In thousands except per share amounts)</p>
<p>			    Three Months Ended  Twelve Months Ended</p>
<p>					December 31,  December 31,</p>
<p>					1996     1995     1996     1995</p>
<p> Net sales			$40,658 $41,213 $130,030 $126,695</p>
<p> Special charges		    489	 0    2,562	  0</p>
<p> Operating income (loss)	  227     885  (5,405)    3,999</p>
<p>Gain (loss) on sale (write-down)</p>
<p>  of investments		(1,582)   1,771  (2,382)    1,771</p>
<p> Net income (loss)	   ( 1,605)   1,428  ( 5,265)   3,113</p>
<p>Earnings per share:</p>
<p> Net income (loss)	     ( .20)    0.17   (0.64)     0.38</p>
<p>Weighted average number of</p>
<p> shares outstanding	     8,208   8,251    8,202    8,236</p>
<p>NOTE: 1996 periods include $400,000 inventory write-down in the 3 months ended 12/31/96 and a $4.9 million inventory write-down in 12 months ended 12/31/96</p>
<p>1995 Q4 and year include a loss of $548,000 from equity interest in unconsolidated affiliate.</p>
<p>1995 gain from investments was from sale of interest in Simmons Outdoor Corp.</p>
<p>12 month results in 1996 were hurt by strength of Swiss franc versus the U.S. dollar, since bulk of its products are purchased in Swiss francs.</p>
<p>((-- New York Newsdesk 212 859-1610))</p>
</text>
